  "duration": 39.5,
  "vo": "A two-dollar Powerball ticket. What's it really worth? Each prize: prize times chance. Add them up. Four bucks, at one in thirty-eight: worth ten cents. Three more small wins: seven cents. Both hundred-dollar prizes: one cent. Fifty grand, at one in nine hundred thirteen thousand: five cents. Less than the four-dollar prize! A million bucks: nine cents. Thirty-two cents so far. Now the jackpot: one in two hundred ninety-two million. Jackpot cash this week: about a hundred ninety-nine point eight million. Minus thirty-seven percent federal tax. Times a one-in-two-hundred-ninety-two-million chance: forty-three cents. Plus the thirty-two cents. So the whole ticket is worth… about seventy-five cents. For two dollars.",
